-- WASH Retreat, part 28: tent cards no longer name the WAP answer. Each source, disposal and latrine
-- points to a helper card, so people scan it to learn the WAP name. The answers do not change.
-- T103, T203 and T301 now use helper card A9 (plastic tank with holes = Cesspit).
update sap_tents set card = '3 people live here, aged 59, 26, 22. The father heads this household. Nobody has a physical disability. Storage at the tent: 3 "five barrel" tanks, plus 4 jerrycans of 20 L. One tank is shared with the neighbours. They drink from the source on helper card B1; for washing they use the source on helper card B6. They pay nothing for water. Kitchen and shower water goes to what you see on helper card A5, desludged twice a year. Inside the shelter: a latrine like helper card C1. Soap is at the handwashing point.' where code = 'T101';
update sap_tents set card = '3 people live here, aged 40, 34, 18. The father heads this household. Nobody has a physical disability. Storage at the tent: 2 × 500 L tank, plus 2 jerrycans of 20 L. One tank is shared with the neighbours. They drink bottled water they buy; for washing they use the source on helper card B2. They pay for their water. Kitchen and shower water goes to what you see on helper card A1. No latrine inside the shelter; they use the shared latrines. Soap is at the handwashing point.' where code = 'T102';
